# Raw upstream downloads. Never committed: too large, and re-fetchable.
raw/
# `build/` is the SHIPPED index and IS committed. That is not a convenience:
# committing it is what makes jsDelivr able to serve it from the public repo for
# free (ADR-0007, ADR-0031). 4 MB byte-identical for every user is exactly the
# traffic pattern that turns Firebase Hosting egress into an unbounded cost at
# $0.15/GB past the 10 GB free tier, so the CDN path is the cheap one and the
# repo is its delivery mechanism.
#
# Commit on index-version bumps only, never per rebuild: the version is in every
# filename, so a bump writes new paths instead of rewriting existing blobs.
#
# build-sample/ is the fixture build, also committed, so a reader can inspect an
# artefact without running the pipeline. It is a SIBLING of build/ rather than a
# subdirectory because sync-datasets.mjs copies build/ recursively into the web
# app's public dir — anything parked under build/ ships to Hosting.
build/full/

# Media binaries. Never committed here: they are published from the media repo
# by the release workflow (ADR-0007, src/media.mjs). ~34 MB for the full set.
build/media/assets/
